.TH LOU_TRANSLATE "1" "September 2026" "Liblouis 3.39.0" "User Commands"
.SH "نام (NAME)"
lou_translate \- A Braille translator for large scale testing of liblouis Braille translation tables
.SH "خلاصه دستور (SYNOPSIS)"
.B lou_translate
[\fI\,OPTIONS\/\fR] \fI\,TABLE\/\fR
.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
Translate whatever is on standard input and print it on standard
output. It is intended for large\-scale testing of the accuracy of
braille translation and back\-translation.
.SS "TABLE is either:"
.TP
\- a query
KEY[:VALUE] [KEY[:VALUE] ...]
.TP
\- a file list
FILE[,FILE,...]
.SH "گزینه‌ها (OPTIONS)"
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
display this help and exit
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
display version information and exit
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-forward\fR
forward translation using the given table
.TP
\fB\-b\fR, \fB\-\-backward\fR
backward translation using the given table
If neither \fB\-f\fR nor \fB\-b\fR are specified forward translation
is assumed
.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-display\-table\fR
use the given display table for the translation. The
display table determines how braille dot patterns are
encoded as text (decoded in case of backward
translation). Without a display table, the braille
encoding is determined by the translation table, when
it is specified as a file list, or Unicode braille when
the table is specified as a query. For clarity and
reliability, it is recommended to always make the
display table explicit.
.SH "مثال‌ها (EXAMPLES)"
.IP
lou_translate language:en grade:2 region:en\-US < input.txt
.IP
Do a forward translation of English text to grade 2 contracted braille
according to the U.S. braille standard.
.IP
lou_translate \-d en\-us\-brf.dis language:en grade:2 region:en\-US < input.txt
.IP
Here we do the same forward translation but with a specific ASCII braille
encoding instead of Unicode braille.
.IP
lou_translate \-d unicode.dis en\-us\-g2.ctb < input.txt
.IP
Do a forward translation with table en\-us\-g2.ctb and Unicode braille encoding.
.IP
echo ",! qk br{n fox" | lou_translate \-b \-d text_nabcc.dis language:en grade:2 region:en\-US
.IP
Do a backward translation with the English grade 2 table. Note that the ASCII
braille input (as shown here) must match the specified display table
(North American Braille Computer Code in this case).
.SH "نویسنده (AUTHOR)"
